finding: The selector misses a real disk input under the cheap guard: src/extras/text/Inter-Regular.ttf. On HEAD, selectGates(await gateInputs(allocationGates()), ["src/extras/text/Inter-Regular.ttf"]) returns [], while allocation.ts:251 copies that file into every sampler bundle and Text loads it at initialization. Independently reproduced in an archive of HEAD at /tmp/shallot-review-font.3SNWnY (node_modules symlink only): replacing only this font with an empty file makes bun test ./src/extras/text/layout-allocation.node.ts fail with allocation sampler exited 1, Plugin "Text" initialize threw: font 0 ... failed to load. Thus an input reaching a gate can change without selecting it; the six new tests all pass despite this hole. This is not the accepted crates/physics gap. Include runtime/copied assets in dependency selection or conservatively select their consumers.
